WEBVTT

1
00:01:08.240 --> 00:01:12.000
"HEARTS ARE MADE TO BE BROKEN."
OSCAR WILDE

2
00:01:38.480 --> 00:01:42.280
-So this is your palace?
-It’s more like my museum.

3
00:01:42.440 --> 00:01:43.920
I love your house.

4
00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:47.640
It was my grandfather’s.
He built it.

5
00:01:49.360 --> 00:01:51.760
-Have you always lived here?
-All my life.

6
00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:54.840
This house is as much mine
as I am its.

7
00:01:55.880 --> 00:01:58.240
-Does it work?
-What?

8
00:01:59.160 --> 00:02:01.280
Saying those grandiose phrases
to hook up.

9
00:02:01.440 --> 00:02:03.760
"This house is as much mine
as I am its".

10
00:02:04.840 --> 00:02:05.960
No. I’m serious.

11
00:02:07.280 --> 00:02:10.160
Years ago. my grandfather’s family
owned almost all this area.

12
00:02:10.640 --> 00:02:13.200
When my parents died.
I got the house.

13
00:02:13.360 --> 00:02:15.760
and my sisters got everything else.

14
00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:20.160
-Guess how long it took to sell it all.
-Ten minutes?

15
00:02:21.680 --> 00:02:23.520
-Not that long.
-And they made a fortune.

16
00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:25.720
No. A mega-fortune.

17
00:02:27.240 --> 00:02:30.080
The house is impressive.
but maybe you lost out.

18
00:02:31.720 --> 00:02:33.160
I’m not interested in money.

19
00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:38.360
I care more about my daughters.
my work. Money is...

20
00:02:39.080 --> 00:02:39.920
boring.

21
00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:43.800
A little money is boring.

22
00:02:46.920 --> 00:02:47.800
Is it real?

23
00:02:48.720 --> 00:02:50.400
Everything in this house is real.

24
00:02:51.360 --> 00:02:53.120
-Do you know Eric Clapton?
-Yes.

25
00:02:53.800 --> 00:02:55.800
but Miguel Ríos gave me that guitar.

26
00:02:56.480 --> 00:02:57.600
Are you friends?

27
00:02:59.160 --> 00:03:01.480
I produced
Rock en el País de las Maravillas.

28
00:03:01.640 --> 00:03:03.480
A good album.
Did you make a mega-fortune?

29
00:03:03.640 --> 00:03:05.400
No. just a fortune.

30
00:03:10.960 --> 00:03:11.680
That tree

31
00:03:12.320 --> 00:03:14.000
is my favorite place in the house.

32
00:03:15.520 --> 00:03:17.320
I gave my first kiss of love there.

33
00:03:18.080 --> 00:03:19.200
And what was it like?

34
00:03:20.120 --> 00:03:21.600
Was it something like this?

35
00:03:33.840 --> 00:03:36.920
My grandfather always told me
that it was a magic tree

36
00:03:37.600 --> 00:03:39.920
and long ago this was a sacred forest

37
00:03:42.080 --> 00:03:46.240
and nymphs. spirits and witches
lived in its trees.

38
00:03:46.400 --> 00:03:47.320
How interesting.

39
00:03:48.840 --> 00:03:51.680
and I’m sure it was
a fantastic place for fucking.

40
00:04:26.520 --> 00:04:28.360
THE HANGED WOMAN

41
00:04:51.680 --> 00:04:54.920
No. she wasn’t my girlfriend.
We saw each other occasionally.

42
00:04:56.360 --> 00:04:59.320
-How long did the relationship last?
-It wasn’t a relationship.

43
00:05:00.120 --> 00:05:02.760
It was just sex.
And it was a few months.

44
00:05:03.560 --> 00:05:04.840
What were you? Fuck buddies?

45
00:05:07.280 --> 00:05:10.360
She was a singer-songwriter.
We ended it a month ago.

46
00:05:10.520 --> 00:05:12.280
but she insisted on carrying on.

47
00:05:13.960 --> 00:05:15.600
So you left her.

48
00:05:16.400 --> 00:05:18.400
I stopped answering her messages.

49
00:05:19.680 --> 00:05:23.240
She kept insisting. so I told her
I was seeing someone else now.

50
00:05:25.720 --> 00:05:26.600
Her?

51
00:05:27.800 --> 00:05:30.360
No. I met her tonight.

52
00:05:31.280 --> 00:05:35.120
-Did you come straight from the concert?
-Yes. we did.

53
00:05:35.280 --> 00:05:36.560
Did you know the victim?

54
00:05:37.080 --> 00:05:40.920
I have no idea who she is.
It’s my first time in this house.

55
00:05:41.600 --> 00:05:43.120
Since what time have you been with him?

56
00:05:44.440 --> 00:05:46.440
Well. all evening.

57
00:05:47.840 --> 00:05:51.360
-Was there anyone else in the house?
-No. just the two of us.

58
00:05:51.520 --> 00:05:54.520
My daughters are with their mother.
We have shared custody.

59
00:05:55.440 --> 00:05:57.200
I never play at home
when they’re with me.

60
00:05:58.440 --> 00:05:59.560
Playing at home.

61
00:06:00.920 --> 00:06:02.600
You know what I mean.

62
00:06:04.520 --> 00:06:08.920
-Did your daughters know her?
-No. they’re 9 and 15 years old.

63
00:06:09.080 --> 00:06:12.800
Honestly. I’d prefer
if they knew nothing about this.

64
00:06:13.840 --> 00:06:14.640
You are

65
00:06:16.200 --> 00:06:17.480
very considerate.

66
00:06:18.200 --> 00:06:21.080
So was she. hanging herself
when they weren’t here.

67
00:06:22.040 --> 00:06:23.960
Imagine if they’d found her.

68
00:06:32.840 --> 00:06:35.360
Well. you’ll have to look after him.

69
00:06:35.520 --> 00:06:38.520
Of course I will.
And I’ll introduce him to dad.

70
00:06:40.560 --> 00:06:42.120
-Bye. Mom!
-Bye.

71
00:06:42.280 --> 00:06:43.400
-Hello. girls.
-Hello!

72
00:06:46.360 --> 00:06:47.240
Hello. Dad!

73
00:06:48.720 --> 00:06:49.960
And this canary?

74
00:06:50.120 --> 00:06:53.960
It’s a nightingale
and I’m looking after him.

75
00:06:56.280 --> 00:06:59.360
It’s a lovely nightingale.
Where did he come from?

76
00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:01.720
Patti found it injured in the forest.

77
00:07:02.760 --> 00:07:03.720
Why didn’t you bring Marley?

78
00:07:04.320 --> 00:07:07.160
Because he’s my dog
and his custody isn’t shared.

79
00:07:09.800 --> 00:07:10.560
Stay for supper.

80
00:07:11.360 --> 00:07:13.040
I’ve ordered sushi from Rashomon.

81
00:07:13.200 --> 00:07:14.120
I’m not hungry.

82
00:07:14.960 --> 00:07:16.560
It’s your favorite restaurant.

83
00:07:17.800 --> 00:07:18.640
Not anymore.

84
00:07:20.320 --> 00:07:22.920
And I don’t like them
spending time in this house.

85
00:07:25.080 --> 00:07:26.360
This house is their house.

86
00:07:28.400 --> 00:07:30.360
Don’t bring women when they’re here.

87
00:07:31.560 --> 00:07:32.880
You know I never do.

88
00:07:33.040 --> 00:07:35.080
You never play at home. right?

89
00:07:36.320 --> 00:07:37.240
Who told you that?

90
00:07:38.680 --> 00:07:39.560
The police.

91
00:07:40.920 --> 00:07:42.600
Did you think
they wouldn’t talk to me?

92
00:07:42.760 --> 00:07:45.000
I’m amazed they didn’t
interrogate the children.

93
00:07:46.160 --> 00:07:47.760
Fuck whoever you want!

94
00:07:48.280 --> 00:07:49.680
Like when we were married.

95
00:07:50.360 --> 00:07:53.480
but they can’t kill themselves
in the garden where my children play.

96
00:08:00.040 --> 00:08:02.960
Pretty. so pretty. my beautiful Oscar.

97
00:08:04.680 --> 00:08:06.640
Pretty. so pretty. my gentle Oscar.

98
00:08:08.840 --> 00:08:09.680
Fly sweetly.

99
00:08:11.240 --> 00:08:12.120
Fly blue.

100
00:08:20.520 --> 00:08:22.520
-How’s the cake?
-Delicious.

101
00:08:22.680 --> 00:08:24.480
-Did you make it?
-Of course.

102
00:08:25.440 --> 00:08:27.720
-You’re lying to us.
-Of course.

103
00:08:29.800 --> 00:08:30.640
Dad...

104
00:08:32.040 --> 00:08:33.240
Do you know who Rebeca is?

105
00:08:33.960 --> 00:08:35.680
Rebeca? I have no idea.

106
00:08:36.240 --> 00:08:40.480
I found this on the couch.
And look. it says Rebeca.

107
00:08:40.640 --> 00:08:41.560
Give me that.

108
00:08:41.720 --> 00:08:42.760
-She’s your girlfriend.
-No.

109
00:08:42.920 --> 00:08:43.920
She’s one of them.

110
00:08:44.080 --> 00:08:45.040
And you two?

111
00:08:45.560 --> 00:08:46.680
Have you got boyfriends?

112
00:08:46.840 --> 00:08:47.720
Janis does!

113
00:08:47.880 --> 00:08:48.800
Shut up!

114
00:08:48.960 --> 00:08:51.200
-His name is Dani.
-Patti!

115
00:08:51.360 --> 00:08:54.080
-What Dani is that?
-He’s nobody.

116
00:08:54.240 --> 00:08:56.000
-Is she lying to us?
-Of course.

117
00:08:56.160 --> 00:08:57.400
I don’t have a boyfriend.

118
00:08:57.560 --> 00:08:59.600
OK. OK. I’ll be quiet.

119
00:09:01.200 --> 00:09:02.200
Is it Daniel Reyes?

120
00:09:03.360 --> 00:09:05.560
-Our neighbor across the way.
-How do you know?

121
00:09:06.520 --> 00:09:08.120
A little bird told me.

122
00:09:08.720 --> 00:09:09.440
Tweet tweet.

123
00:09:09.600 --> 00:09:11.000
Is he called Oscar?

124
00:09:11.160 --> 00:09:12.720
Who’s Oscar? Patti’s boyfriend?

125
00:09:12.880 --> 00:09:14.920
-No.
-Her parrot.

126
00:09:15.080 --> 00:09:17.560
-He’s a nightingale.
-Your boyfriend is a nightingale?

127
00:09:18.320 --> 00:09:20.280
-Yes.
-She’s even written a song about him.

128
00:09:20.440 --> 00:09:21.920
I have the words. but not the music.

129
00:09:23.160 --> 00:09:25.560
Heavens.
But what a coincidence!

130
00:09:26.360 --> 00:09:27.240
A piano!

131
00:09:28.080 --> 00:09:29.480
-Shall I help you?
-Come on!

132
00:09:32.240 --> 00:09:33.080
-OK?
-OK.

133
00:09:37.720 --> 00:09:38.600
OK?

134
00:09:38.760 --> 00:09:41.040
-Pretty. so pretty...
-Again.

135
00:09:41.200 --> 00:09:46.480
Pretty. so pretty. my beautiful Oscar.

136
00:09:46.640 --> 00:09:51.480
Pretty. so pretty. my gentle Oscar.

137
00:09:51.640 --> 00:09:52.560
Janis. the guitar.

138
00:09:53.280 --> 00:09:57.760
Pretty. so pretty. my beautiful Oscar.

139
00:09:57.920 --> 00:10:02.440
Pretty. so pretty. my gentle...

140
00:10:04.120 --> 00:10:05.000
Oscar!

141
00:10:05.160 --> 00:10:06.400
Janis. don’t open the door!

142
00:10:06.560 --> 00:10:07.600
Janis. Janis!

143
00:10:14.680 --> 00:10:15.520
Oscar!

144
00:10:16.360 --> 00:10:17.240
Oscar!

145
00:10:20.200 --> 00:10:23.200
Don’t worry. sweetheart.
He’ll be in the garden.

146
00:10:24.240 --> 00:10:26.200
sleeping in the tree
or in the rose garden.

147
00:10:26.760 --> 00:10:30.040
We’ll look for him in daylight
and I’m sure we’ll find him.

148
00:10:31.680 --> 00:10:32.520
What if he’s gone?

149
00:10:34.200 --> 00:10:38.080
He was injured. I don’t think
he could have flown over the wall.

150
00:10:40.640 --> 00:10:42.000
What if a cat ate him?

151
00:10:43.760 --> 00:10:45.600
Oscar looks pretty smart.

152
00:10:46.440 --> 00:10:49.000
If we haven’t found him.
a cat won’t catch him.

153
00:10:50.040 --> 00:10:51.880
Maybe he’s playing hide and seek.

154
00:10:52.960 --> 00:10:53.760
Dad.

155
00:10:54.680 --> 00:10:57.320
you know that nightingales
don’t do that.

156
00:11:00.280 --> 00:11:02.680
You’ll see.
tomorrow he’ll sing you awake.

157
00:11:03.800 --> 00:11:05.680
-Are you lying?
-No.

158
00:11:06.600 --> 00:11:09.080
Tomorrow we’ll find him
and I’ll help you cure him.

159
00:11:09.960 --> 00:11:11.760
OK? Now go to sleep.

160
00:11:35.040 --> 00:11:35.840
Oscar!

161
00:11:49.680 --> 00:11:50.520
Oscar?

162
00:11:52.680 --> 00:11:54.800
Oscar. come down here.
Come on.

163
00:12:19.080 --> 00:12:20.920
You’re never to escape again.

164
00:12:21.960 --> 00:12:22.720
Hello.

165
00:12:25.400 --> 00:12:26.560
Dad!

166
00:12:30.760 --> 00:12:31.560
Patti!

167
00:12:40.400 --> 00:12:41.400
What are you doing there?

168
00:12:43.760 --> 00:12:44.640
I climbed up for Oscar.

169
00:12:49.840 --> 00:12:50.960
Come down. please.

170
00:12:52.200 --> 00:12:54.120
You climbed a tree at night?

171
00:12:56.320 --> 00:12:58.920
You could have fallen
and killed yourself.

172
00:12:59.680 --> 00:13:01.040
And goodbye. vacation.

173
00:13:02.440 --> 00:13:05.360
There was a lady in the tree.
but she isn’t there now.

174
00:13:05.520 --> 00:13:07.400
Patti. it was a dream.

175
00:13:08.720 --> 00:13:09.840
another one of your dreams.

176
00:13:10.400 --> 00:13:12.520
Janis. you and I are the only ones here.

177
00:13:13.520 --> 00:13:15.280
She’d hurt her neck.

178
00:13:15.440 --> 00:13:19.200
Don’t worry. Dad. last week
she dreamed I shot myself in the head.

179
00:13:19.360 --> 00:13:20.920
And I’d just got extensions!

180
00:13:22.600 --> 00:13:24.760
OK. I see that you don’t believe me.

181
00:13:25.680 --> 00:13:27.360
-Patti!
-I’m going to play with Oscar.

182
00:13:31.120 --> 00:13:33.760
-Why did you tell her?
-Tell her what?

183
00:13:34.360 --> 00:13:36.880
What your mother told you
when she shouldn’t have.

184
00:13:37.400 --> 00:13:38.480
Mom didn’t tell me anything.

185
00:13:39.560 --> 00:13:40.760
Janis. please.

186
00:13:42.160 --> 00:13:43.120
Dad. what happened?

187
00:13:49.400 --> 00:13:50.200
Dad?

188
00:13:52.240 --> 00:13:54.120
Ana. don’t deny it.

189
00:13:54.280 --> 00:13:57.280
Patti said she saw a lady in the tree
with a wound on her neck.

190
00:13:57.440 --> 00:13:59.000
It’s obvious you told them.

191
00:13:59.160 --> 00:14:01.240
It must be another one of her nightmares.

192
00:14:01.400 --> 00:14:04.840
Yes. but that nightmare is based
on something you told them.

193
00:14:05.000 --> 00:14:06.400
I didn’t tell them anything.

194
00:14:06.560 --> 00:14:08.480
Then they heard you telling someone.

195
00:14:09.040 --> 00:14:12.520
I’ve only spoken to the police.
but they weren’t in the house.

196
00:14:13.400 --> 00:14:16.240
If she has another nightmare
we’ll take her to her psychologist..

197
00:14:16.720 --> 00:14:18.400
And you should go back to yours.

198
00:14:18.560 --> 00:14:21.080
Don’t worry. I usually do
every time I talk to you.

199
00:14:24.920 --> 00:14:25.640
Patti.

200
00:14:27.080 --> 00:14:30.040
Dani told me that two weeks ago
a woman hanged herself in that tree.

201
00:14:31.320 --> 00:14:32.640
One of Dad’s girlfriends.

202
00:14:50.040 --> 00:14:52.800
Her name was Rosa Martín.
but she called herself The Hanged Woman.

203
00:14:53.840 --> 00:14:55.320
My mother filmed this.

204
00:14:56.800 --> 00:14:58.120
I got it off her phone.

205
00:15:00.280 --> 00:15:01.680
She saw her going in several times.

206
00:15:02.520 --> 00:15:04.240
Well. her and lots of others.

207
00:15:06.400 --> 00:15:07.680
Dad needs a psychiatrist.

208
00:15:12.080 --> 00:15:12.840
What?

209
00:15:13.400 --> 00:15:15.120
Is this the woman you saw in the tree?

210
00:15:19.560 --> 00:15:20.320
Yes.

211
00:15:21.200 --> 00:15:22.080
Yes. it’s her.

212
00:15:41.240 --> 00:15:42.360
What the hell is that?

213
00:15:43.960 --> 00:15:44.840
Wait a minute.

214
00:15:46.080 --> 00:15:46.920
I won’t be long.

215
00:15:54.400 --> 00:15:58.320
Pretty. so pretty.
you’re a nuisance. Oscar.

216
00:16:13.720 --> 00:16:14.560
Fran.

217
00:16:16.800 --> 00:16:17.560
Fran!

218
00:16:25.520 --> 00:16:26.240
Fran?

219
00:16:52.000 --> 00:16:52.760
Fran?

220
00:17:09.240 --> 00:17:10.080
Look at me.

221
00:18:28.320 --> 00:18:29.160
Oscar!

222
00:18:34.560 --> 00:18:35.760
What the hell have you done?

223
00:18:42.240 --> 00:18:43.040
Hello. Dad!

224
00:18:43.200 --> 00:18:45.280
-Hi! Did you have a good time?
-Where’s Oscar?

225
00:18:45.440 --> 00:18:48.040
Sweetheart. I have to tell you something
that will make you a bit sad.

226
00:18:54.080 --> 00:18:55.840
I got up this morning
and the poor bird...

227
00:18:56.000 --> 00:18:57.760
He isn’t a bird.
he’s a nightingale!

228
00:18:58.320 --> 00:19:00.600
He was hurt and you promised
to look after him!

229
00:19:00.760 --> 00:19:04.000
-Now he’s dead and it’s your fault!
-I know. love. but...

230
00:19:04.160 --> 00:19:05.240
Leave me alone!

231
00:19:07.160 --> 00:19:09.160
Maybe we can bury him
in the rose garden.

232
00:19:10.960 --> 00:19:12.600
Who were you with last night. Dad?

233
00:19:13.240 --> 00:19:16.360
I took him out to the porch a moment
for some air

234
00:19:16.520 --> 00:19:18.000
and this morning I found him like this.

235
00:19:18.160 --> 00:19:20.840
You left him out there all night?
Was he such a nuisance?

236
00:19:22.560 --> 00:19:25.400
-I’m not surprised Mom left.
-Look. Janis...

237
00:19:27.080 --> 00:19:28.280
Janis. please.

238
00:19:49.480 --> 00:19:50.560
Don’t be scared.

239
00:19:51.720 --> 00:19:53.040
I just want to be your friend.

240
00:19:56.520 --> 00:19:57.600
Your name is...

241
00:19:58.960 --> 00:20:00.200
Patti. isn’t it?

242
00:20:01.960 --> 00:20:02.840
And you can see me.

243
00:20:04.560 --> 00:20:06.120
No one can see me
if I don’t want them to.

244
00:20:09.720 --> 00:20:12.320
When I was your age I was like you.

245
00:20:14.080 --> 00:20:17.160
So I guess we’re both special.
don’t you think?

246
00:20:19.240 --> 00:20:20.000
Who are you?

247
00:20:22.640 --> 00:20:24.000
What happened to your nightingale?

248
00:20:25.840 --> 00:20:26.680
What happened to Oscar?

249
00:20:28.800 --> 00:20:30.160
How do you know his name is Oscar?

250
00:20:31.440 --> 00:20:34.000
I hear you calling him.
and singing to him.

251
00:20:36.240 --> 00:20:37.960
I called him Oscar for Oscar Wilde.

252
00:20:38.120 --> 00:20:39.640
For The Nightingale and the Rose?

253
00:20:42.120 --> 00:20:44.320
-It’s my favorite story.
-Mine too.

254
00:20:46.120 --> 00:20:46.920
But

255
00:20:48.480 --> 00:20:51.160
I always cry when the nightingale dies.

256
00:20:53.120 --> 00:20:54.960
Now they’ll tell me that Oscar is fine

257
00:20:55.120 --> 00:20:58.280
and that he’ll live happily
in the heaven for birds.

258
00:21:01.240 --> 00:21:02.600
What if we bring him back?

259
00:21:06.640 --> 00:21:07.360
