Here.

532
00:41:16.000 --> 00:41:16.800
What happened?

533
00:41:17.840 --> 00:41:18.880
Mind the glass...

534
00:41:36.160 --> 00:41:37.840
Marley...

535
00:41:39.280 --> 00:41:41.120
Marley...

536
00:41:56.640 --> 00:41:57.520
You’re all wet.

537
00:42:00.280 --> 00:42:01.080
Were you swimming?

538
00:42:53.560 --> 00:42:54.360
Patti?

539
00:42:54.520 --> 00:42:55.400
What’s wrong?

540
00:42:56.040 --> 00:42:56.920
You’re soaking wet.

541
00:43:00.440 --> 00:43:03.520
I have to tell you something
that will make you very sad.

542
00:43:04.560 --> 00:43:05.520
Patti believes

543
00:43:05.680 --> 00:43:07.680
that the woman who hanged herself
in the garden

544
00:43:07.840 --> 00:43:09.360
is a ghost who lives in the house.

545
00:43:10.200 --> 00:43:13.360
She cured her bird.
she saved us from the thieves.

546
00:43:13.520 --> 00:43:15.080
she bewitched Silvia.

547
00:43:15.240 --> 00:43:18.760
and she killed Marley
because his barking broke her spell.

548
00:43:19.400 --> 00:43:21.880
And the worst thing is
that now Janis believes it too.

549
00:43:23.640 --> 00:43:25.880
Traumatic events generate energies

550
00:43:26.040 --> 00:43:29.120
that can provoke
situations of collective hysteria.

551
00:43:29.840 --> 00:43:31.480
but at times that can be reversed.

552
00:43:32.320 --> 00:43:33.160
How?

553
00:43:33.320 --> 00:43:35.400
I know people
who cleanse those energies.

554
00:43:36.320 --> 00:43:37.160
Witches?

555
00:43:39.160 --> 00:43:40.440
Parapsychologists.

556
00:43:40.600 --> 00:43:42.360
I don’t really believe in those things.

557
00:43:43.600 --> 00:43:44.600
Patti does.

558
00:43:53.560 --> 00:43:55.080
She killed Marley.

559
00:43:56.600 --> 00:43:58.160
She’s hiding somewhere.

560
00:43:58.720 --> 00:44:00.280
We have to throw her out of here.

561
00:44:01.360 --> 00:44:03.240
And I think I know how to do it.

562
00:44:04.640 --> 00:44:05.720
She taught me.

563
00:44:06.560 --> 00:44:08.520
We have to use blood and fire.

564
00:44:09.360 --> 00:44:11.960
We need things of hers
to burn them.

565
00:44:12.120 --> 00:44:12.920
Dani.

566
00:44:13.080 --> 00:44:14.560
We have to burn everything.

567
00:44:14.720 --> 00:44:15.520
Give it to me.

568
00:44:15.680 --> 00:44:17.240
I’ve made a doll that looks like her.

569
00:44:19.640 --> 00:44:20.680
Between the three of us.

570
00:44:21.400 --> 00:44:22.640
we can make her go away.

571
00:44:31.520 --> 00:44:32.360
Rosa?

572
00:44:33.120 --> 00:44:33.920
Are you there?

573
00:44:35.720 --> 00:44:37.600
We want to talk to you.

574
00:44:48.120 --> 00:44:49.440
You are hurting me.

575
00:44:49.600 --> 00:44:50.840
And you hurt my mother.

576
00:44:51.320 --> 00:44:52.160
And Marley.

577
00:44:55.000 --> 00:44:56.360
Marley drowned.

578
00:44:57.320 --> 00:44:58.080
No.

579
00:44:58.240 --> 00:44:59.480
No. you killed him.

580
00:44:59.920 --> 00:45:00.800
Why?

581
00:45:01.480 --> 00:45:02.560
Why did you kill Marley?

582
00:45:04.960 --> 00:45:06.120
Why did you kill Oscar?

583
00:45:11.320 --> 00:45:12.360
Leave this house!

584
00:45:12.520 --> 00:45:13.440
Go away!

585
00:45:17.320 --> 00:45:18.280
Go away!

586
00:45:18.440 --> 00:45:19.600
Go away now!

587
00:45:19.760 --> 00:45:20.680
Go away!

588
00:45:20.840 --> 00:45:21.680
Stop.

589
00:45:26.840 --> 00:45:27.640
Go in.

590
00:45:40.480 --> 00:45:41.320
Dani!

591
00:45:41.480 --> 00:45:42.680
Dani. are you all right?

592
00:45:44.360 --> 00:45:46.160
Dad. he needs to go to hospital!

593
00:45:55.960 --> 00:46:00.480
Don’t take this badly. but all this
looks to me like science fiction.

594
00:46:00.640 --> 00:46:03.160
I told Dr. Durán
I don’t believe in ghosts.

595
00:46:04.080 --> 00:46:05.360
But you do believe in physics.

596
00:46:06.640 --> 00:46:07.600
In energies.

597
00:46:09.240 --> 00:46:11.480
Traumatic events have happened here.

598
00:46:12.440 --> 00:46:16.720
-What are you going to do exactly?
-Well. however odd it may seem.

599
00:46:17.720 --> 00:46:21.120
we’re going to try to reverse
the residual psychic energy

600
00:46:21.280 --> 00:46:22.360
left by those events.

601
00:46:23.440 --> 00:46:25.160
I hope it reassures my daughters.

602
00:46:25.800 --> 00:46:28.440
They’re obsessed by what’s happened.
especially the little one.

603
00:46:28.840 --> 00:46:29.720
Patti. right?

604
00:46:30.680 --> 00:46:31.600
Her name is Patti.

605
00:46:33.120 --> 00:46:35.720
-And you are...?
-May I walk through your garden?

606
00:46:48.240 --> 00:46:49.080
Hello.

607
00:46:57.320 --> 00:46:58.440
I’m Begoña.

608
00:47:02.280 --> 00:47:03.160
Can you see me?

609
00:47:04.320 --> 00:47:06.760
Yes. I’ve always been able
to see those like you.

610
00:47:07.680 --> 00:47:09.200
The dead. you mean?

611
00:47:10.480 --> 00:47:12.920
I prefer to call you persons in transit.

612
00:47:14.920 --> 00:47:15.640
Right.

613
00:47:16.280 --> 00:47:17.880
But I’m not in transit.

614
00:47:18.360 --> 00:47:19.240
I live here.

615
00:47:20.440 --> 00:47:21.800
You killed yourself here.

616
00:47:25.480 --> 00:47:26.480
You should leave.

617
00:47:27.600 --> 00:47:29.680
That would be best
for everyone. wouldn’t it?

618
00:47:29.840 --> 00:47:31.480
Especially for you.

619
00:47:32.760 --> 00:47:36.200
And where should I go?
To Heaven. to Hell?

620
00:47:36.360 --> 00:47:38.040
You’re causing a lot of pain.

621
00:47:41.840 --> 00:47:43.320
They caused me pain too.

622
00:47:47.720 --> 00:47:48.560
What’s she doing?

623
00:47:49.360 --> 00:47:50.800
At times we work with her.

624
00:47:51.280 --> 00:47:52.680
She’s a very powerful medium.

625
00:47:54.280 --> 00:47:57.360
We’re lucky to have her here.
She’s going to Africa tomorrow.

626
00:48:02.760 --> 00:48:05.800
I think you don’t even know
if you love him or hate him.

627
00:48:06.560 --> 00:48:07.720
Is there a difference?

628
00:48:11.000 --> 00:48:12.880
I’ve seen other cases like yours.

629
00:48:14.280 --> 00:48:18.360
The longer you’re here.
the more you’ll lose touch with reality.

630
00:48:19.960 --> 00:48:21.920
Soon only your obsession will be left.

631
00:48:23.760 --> 00:48:26.600
That obsession
which destroyed your life

632
00:48:27.880 --> 00:48:29.680
will end up destroying your soul.

633
00:48:31.720 --> 00:48:32.760
My soul...

634
00:48:36.520 --> 00:48:38.120
Why don’t you worry about yours?

635
00:49:07.680 --> 00:49:11.080
You hanged yourself here.
It must have hurt a lot.

636
00:49:12.960 --> 00:49:14.000
Have you seen my death?

637
00:49:14.880 --> 00:49:18.560
You have to leave.
I can help you transition. trust me.

638
00:49:18.720 --> 00:49:19.600
You know what?

639
00:49:21.640 --> 00:49:23.040
I want to see yours too.

640
00:49:49.880 --> 00:49:52.360
Don’t look him in the eye.

641
00:50:01.760 --> 00:50:04.880
Our blood is stronger than yours.

642
00:50:05.800 --> 00:50:08.960
Shangó. I invoke the name of Shangó!

643
00:50:09.520 --> 00:50:11.560
I am the God of Thunder.

644
00:50:12.200 --> 00:50:13.680
I am Thunder.

645
00:50:13.840 --> 00:50:14.600
Leave.

646
00:50:15.480 --> 00:50:16.280
Leave!

647
00:50:25.960 --> 00:50:28.320
This is my axe!

648
00:50:28.800 --> 00:50:33.160
I am Fire. I am Lightning. I am Shangó!

649
00:50:33.600 --> 00:50:37.200
Shangó's axe is hitting you!

650
00:50:55.920 --> 00:50:57.160
No. no!

651
00:51:05.240 --> 00:51:06.920
It seems you’re going to die in Africa.

652
00:51:07.640 --> 00:51:11.120
Perhaps. but I must help a child.
Let me help you.

653
00:51:11.280 --> 00:51:12.480
I’m not leaving this house

654
00:51:13.440 --> 00:51:14.600
and you can’t make me.

655
00:51:16.480 --> 00:51:17.760
I supposed you’d say that.

656
00:51:21.560 --> 00:51:24.040
I’ve drawn a circle of blood around you.

657
00:51:24.720 --> 00:51:26.760
Now my blood ties you to this tree.

658
00:51:36.720 --> 00:51:37.520
You want to stay?

659
00:51:38.600 --> 00:51:39.360
All right. stay.

660
00:51:40.080 --> 00:51:41.800
But I won’t let you do more harm.

661
00:51:44.400 --> 00:51:47.680
You killed yourself on the tree
and you’ll live in the tree.

662
00:52:31.520 --> 00:52:32.560
Don’t worry.

663
00:52:33.680 --> 00:52:34.680
She isn’t here anymore.

664
00:53:06.160 --> 00:53:08.360
All that was a year ago.

665
00:53:10.400 --> 00:53:13.440
I remember it
as a nightmare we all had.

666
00:53:14.400 --> 00:53:15.440
but it ended.

667
00:53:17.520 --> 00:53:18.840
Patti doesn’t see ghosts.

668
00:53:20.400 --> 00:53:22.240
Janis and Dani are still dating.

669
00:53:22.960 --> 00:53:24.240
they saved his eye.

670
00:53:26.040 --> 00:53:29.320
Well. it seems the parapsychologists
did the trick.

671
00:53:32.000 --> 00:53:34.960
They told me that the medium
died a few days later

672
00:53:35.120 --> 00:53:36.920
on a humanitarian mission in Africa.

673
00:53:41.120 --> 00:53:42.440
Are you still going to therapy?

674
00:53:43.720 --> 00:53:44.960
Twice a week.

675
00:53:47.200 --> 00:53:48.360
I’ve learned a lot.

676
00:53:50.320 --> 00:53:52.080
I’ve regretted a lot.

677
00:53:54.960 --> 00:53:58.680
The girls have told me
that recently you’re a model dad.

678
00:53:59.320 --> 00:54:02.480
Great. because I asked them
to use that expression.

679
00:54:03.880 --> 00:54:05.640
They told me that too.

680
00:54:06.920 --> 00:54:08.400
Is that the same swing?

681
00:54:09.720 --> 00:54:12.440
The same one you swung on
when you were a child.

682
00:54:13.160 --> 00:54:14.040
Heavens.

683
00:54:15.840 --> 00:54:17.320
And when did it break?

684
00:54:17.480 --> 00:54:20.120
May 13. 1997.

685
00:54:20.800 --> 00:54:22.600
The day I turned 16.

686
00:54:22.760 --> 00:54:25.040
The day we kissed for the first time.

687
00:54:25.800 --> 00:54:26.600
I don’t remember.

688
00:54:27.280 --> 00:54:28.440
Are you lying?

689
00:54:28.960 --> 00:54:29.760
Of course.

690
00:54:31.680 --> 00:54:32.960
You leaned on the tree.

691
00:54:33.640 --> 00:54:34.480
I went over

692
00:54:35.200 --> 00:54:36.080
and I kissed you.

693
00:54:36.840 --> 00:54:39.480
Well. it isn’t our tree anymore.

694
00:54:40.040 --> 00:54:40.840
Yes. it is.

695
00:54:45.240 --> 00:54:46.320
And so is the house.

696
00:54:48.960 --> 00:54:50.560
I wouldn’t live there again.

697
00:54:52.600 --> 00:54:53.560
Then we’ll sell it.

698
00:54:54.760 --> 00:54:55.560
What?

699
00:54:58.280 --> 00:54:59.840
If I’ve learned anything about you.

700
00:55:00.000 --> 00:55:02.240
it’s that your life is meaningless
without that house.

701
00:55:04.360 --> 00:55:06.000
If I’ve learned anything about me.

702
00:55:06.920 --> 00:55:09.160
it’s that my life is meaningless
without you.

703
00:55:12.000 --> 00:55:13.480
Aren’t you going a bit fast?

704
00:55:14.840 --> 00:55:18.280
You’re right. we’ve only known
each other for forty years.

705
00:55:20.240 --> 00:55:23.600
Why don’t you stay for supper
and we’ll get better acquainted?

706
00:55:29.120 --> 00:55:34.720
I know it no longer matters
about the questions that I failed

707
00:55:34.880 --> 00:55:40.400
and when I try to correct myself
you won’t be there.

708
00:55:42.560 --> 00:55:48.240
I know that you don’t care
if I can no longer breathe.

709
00:55:48.400 --> 00:55:54.080
and if I choke
I know that you won’t save me.

710
00:55:56.120 --> 00:56:01.800
You have something within you.
I have seen it shine.

711
00:56:02.320 --> 00:56:04.880
but you run away.

712
00:56:09.800 --> 00:56:15.320
Miss me.
don’t fail me this time.

713
00:56:15.480 --> 00:56:20.400
because I don’t know if I’ll be back.

714
00:56:31.960 --> 00:56:34.520
-Is Mom going to stay?
-I hope so.

715
00:56:35.840 --> 00:56:36.680
Forever?

716
00:56:39.040 --> 00:56:39.920
I hope so.

717
00:56:44.040 --> 00:56:45.600
She doesn’t want to live here.

718
00:56:48.120 --> 00:56:49.240
You know what?

719
00:56:52.960 --> 00:56:54.720
I’ve decided to sell this house

720
00:56:55.880 --> 00:56:57.320
and buy a nicer one.

721
00:57:00.080 --> 00:57:01.280
Do you think it’s a good idea?

722
00:57:09.600 --> 00:57:10.800
It could be a good idea.

723
00:57:45.080 --> 00:57:45.880
Oscar?

724
00:57:49.920 --> 00:57:50.720
Oscar?

725
00:57:51.600 --> 00:57:52.400
Patti...

726
00:57:55.000 --> 00:57:57.600
Don’t be scared. you’re dreaming.

727
00:57:58.920 --> 00:58:00.600
We’re both dreaming.

728
00:58:01.640 --> 00:58:02.600
What are you doing here?

729
00:58:04.040 --> 00:58:04.960
What do you want?

730
00:58:05.560 --> 00:58:06.840
Just to apologize.

731
00:58:09.120 --> 00:58:11.120
I never wanted to hurt you. really.

732
00:58:12.080 --> 00:58:13.080
I loved your father.

733
00:58:15.680 --> 00:58:17.520
I loved him from
the moment I saw him.

734
00:58:19.200 --> 00:58:20.760
Remember The Nightingale and the Rose?

735
00:58:24.240 --> 00:58:28.240
The nightingale says
that love is better than life.

736
00:58:30.680 --> 00:58:33.400
that his wings are flame-colored.

737
00:58:35.040 --> 00:58:37.040
and his body is colored like flame.

738
00:58:38.640 --> 00:58:42.080
his lips are sweet as honey

739
00:58:43.360 --> 00:58:44.880
and his breath is like frankincense.

740
00:58:48.800 --> 00:58:49.760
I was mistaken.

741
00:58:53.080 --> 00:58:55.640
I thought that my love for your father
was a mutual love.

742
00:58:59.760 --> 00:59:03.640
That his heart froze
when your mother left and I could cure it.

743
00:59:09.040 --> 00:59:09.840
Silly. wasn’t I?

744
00:59:12.080 --> 00:59:14.440
And now you’ll be
a happy family again. Patti.

745
00:59:16.960 --> 00:59:19.640
I know that soon you’ll sell the house
and move away.

746
00:59:21.520 --> 00:59:23.840
I don’t want to be trapped in the tree.

747
00:59:25.840 --> 00:59:26.720
In the tree?

748
00:59:29.320 --> 00:59:30.200
A year ago.

749
00:59:31.120 --> 00:59:33.640
a witch left me
shut away in the tree.

750
00:59:34.400 --> 00:59:38.120
But I want to get out of here!
You have to help me. please.

751
00:59:39.320 --> 00:59:40.200
But I don’t know how!

752
00:59:42.440 --> 00:59:43.320
Touch the mirror.

753
00:59:59.720 --> 01:00:02.440
You have to do what she did.
but in reverse.

754
01:00:04.120 --> 01:00:05.480
Only that will break the spell.

755
01:00:14.400 --> 01:00:19.280
I am your rose of sugar

756
01:00:20.800 --> 01:00:24.720
I am your rose of honey.

757
01:00:42.680 --> 01:00:44.320
What would you like for breakfast?

758
01:00:45.600 --> 01:00:46.400
The usual.

759
01:01:38.560 --> 01:01:39.320
Look at me.

760
01:02:05.360 --> 01:02:06.360
Ana!

761
01:02:06.760 --> 01:02:07.640
Ana!

762
01:02:08.440 --> 01:02:09.440
Ana!

763
01:02:11.240 --> 01:02:12.120
Ana!

764
01:02:12.280 --> 01:02:13.160
Dad?

765
01:02:15.680 --> 01:02:16.520
No!

766
01:02:16.680 --> 01:02:18.120
-Dad?
-No!

767
01:02:18.280 --> 01:02:19.080
What’s wrong?

768
01:02:19.240 --> 01:02:20.480
It’s your mother!

769
01:02:21.600 --> 01:02:22.480
Mom!

770
01:02:22.640 --> 01:02:23.800
Mom. Mom!

771
01:02:24.480 --> 01:02:26.560
Mom. Mom!

772
01:02:29.840 --> 01:02:30.680
Patti!

773
01:02:31.200 --> 01:02:32.040
Patti!

774
01:02:32.840 --> 01:02:35.520
Hurry. hurry!

775
01:02:35.680 --> 01:02:37.400
No. no!

776
01:02:38.640 --> 01:02:40.360
No!

777
01:02:58.920 --> 01:03:03.480
I was keen to finally meet you.
Fran talks a lot about you.

778
01:03:04.200 --> 01:03:05.400
-Does he?
-Yes.

779
01:03:07.320 --> 01:03:09.280
How did you meet Fran?

780
01:03:10.440 --> 01:03:14.200
He came to one
of my first concerts when...

781
01:03:14.360 --> 01:03:16.360
Well. I was still nobody and

782
01:03:17.600 --> 01:03:19.200
I think we fell in love instantly.

783
01:03:21.760 --> 01:03:24.960
That night we made love under the tree.
under his tree.

784
01:03:26.240 --> 01:03:29.080
and a month later I was living here.

785
01:03:30.280 --> 01:03:35.680
Then we got married. and here we are.
They were very happy years.

786
01:03:37.160 --> 01:03:38.800
And productive too?

787
01:03:39.800 --> 01:03:44.160
-Yes. Fran produces all my albums.
-He only produces your albums.

788
01:03:44.320 --> 01:03:46.880
-I think that’s more than enough.
-Yes. yes.

789
01:03:49.360 --> 01:03:50.200
So.

790
01:03:51.160 --> 01:03:52.880
why don’t you tell me
about those dreams?

791
01:03:55.640 --> 01:03:56.640
The dreams.

792
01:03:58.920 --> 01:04:00.680
Well. they started a few days ago.

793
01:04:02.720 --> 01:04:04.680
I dream that I’m in love with Fran.

794
01:04:06.920 --> 01:04:07.760
But...

795
01:04:09.080 --> 01:04:11.480
He doesn’t love you back?

796
01:04:13.080 --> 01:04:13.920
Exactly.

797
01:04:15.400 --> 01:04:16.280
He ignores me.

798
01:04:17.280 --> 01:04:18.040
And

799
01:04:19.160 --> 01:04:21.640
that sends me into a deep depression
and makes me

800
01:04:22.400 --> 01:04:24.520
kill myself. I hang myself.

801
01:04:26.360 --> 01:04:32.040
And my ghost stays in the house
and I make life impossible for everyone.

802
01:04:33.120 --> 01:04:33.920
For Fran.

803
01:04:35.000 --> 01:04:36.120
for his daughters who.

804
01:04:37.560 --> 01:04:39.400
really. I love as if they were my own.

805
01:04:40.200 --> 01:04:41.960
for Marley. the dog.

806
01:04:43.680 --> 01:04:47.880
Last night. I dreamed that I killed Ana.
his ex. but we’re close friends.

807
01:04:48.040 --> 01:04:49.200
She’s like a sister for me.

808
01:04:51.000 --> 01:04:51.920
And

809
01:04:52.600 --> 01:04:55.080
does anyone else appear in your dreams?

810
01:04:56.920 --> 01:05:02.000
Yes. a woman appears.
she sneaks into the house.

811
01:05:05.040 --> 01:05:05.880
Who is she?

812
01:05:07.560 --> 01:05:08.400
I don’t know.

813
01:05:10.440 --> 01:05:12.760
I don’t know. I can’t see her face.

814
01:05:14.640 --> 01:05:16.120
It’s covered. she’s wearing...

815
01:05:17.680 --> 01:05:19.480
It’s an African mask.

816
01:05:20.640 --> 01:05:21.800
Like that one?

817
01:05:25.680 --> 01:05:26.560
Not like it.

818
01:05:27.440 --> 01:05:28.440
it is that one.

819
01:05:29.240 --> 01:05:30.600
Interesting.

820
01:05:31.520 --> 01:05:35.520
It’s a ceremonial mask
made to fight against evil beings.

821
01:05:35.680 --> 01:05:36.720
Did you know that?

822
01:05:37.120 --> 01:05:41.920
I’m sorry. but I’d completely
forgotten about that album.

823
01:05:44.600 --> 01:05:45.440
Who is she?

824
01:05:46.520 --> 01:05:48.400
Is she a thief?

825
01:05:49.280 --> 01:05:50.400
A fan. perhaps?

826
01:05:52.200 --> 01:05:55.160
I don’t think she’s a fan because

827
01:05:56.600 --> 01:05:57.880
she doesn’t want to talk to me.

828
01:05:58.560 --> 01:05:59.800
just to him.

829
01:06:03.320 --> 01:06:04.440
What does she say to him?

830
01:06:07.280 --> 01:06:08.280
I don’t know.

831
01:06:10.400 --> 01:06:12.160
As soon as she sees me she runs off.

832
01:06:14.680 --> 01:06:18.360
And then I chase her and chase her
and I can’t catch her.

833
01:06:19.200 --> 01:06:20.040
She goes into the house

834
01:06:21.440 --> 01:06:25.000
and it seems I’ll catch her
but she locks herself in Patti’s room.

835
01:06:31.640 --> 01:06:32.760
What happens when you go in?

836
01:06:34.600 --> 01:06:36.200
I can’t go into Patti’s room.

837
01:06:37.320 --> 01:06:38.160
Why?

838
01:06:38.640 --> 01:06:39.840
I don’t know. I can’t.

839
01:06:40.000 --> 01:06:41.480
-Patti doesn’t let you.
-I can’t.

840
01:06:53.880 --> 01:06:57.000
Are you sure no one else
appears in your dreams?

841
01:07:06.880 --> 01:07:11.360
There’s a man too. an elderly man.

842
01:07:12.040 --> 01:07:14.000
who is always in the shadows.

843
01:07:14.640 --> 01:07:18.120
He seems harmless.

844
01:07:19.280 --> 01:07:20.680
but I know he isn’t.

845
01:07:21.640 --> 01:07:24.000
I don’t trust him.

846
01:07:25.200 --> 01:07:26.080
He scares me.

847
01:07:28.760 --> 01:07:30.480
And I don’t want him near Fran.

848
01:07:32.520 --> 01:07:33.320
Why?

849
01:07:38.400 --> 01:07:39.680
Because he wants to kill Fran.

850
01:07:46.000 --> 01:07:47.040
He wants to kill Fran.

851
01:07:48.640 --> 01:07:49.560
Go away!

852
01:07:51.600 --> 01:07:53.480
Go away!

853
01:07:53.640 --> 01:07:54.560
Rosa.

854
01:07:55.240 --> 01:07:57.960
I’m very sorry.
I’m not an expert in dreams.

855
01:07:58.680 --> 01:08:02.440
Maybe you should speak
to another therapist.

856
01:08:05.800 --> 01:08:06.560
What?

857
01:08:08.880 --> 01:08:10.960
You should see another therapist...

858
01:08:15.280 --> 01:08:16.920
Then why have you come?

859
01:08:19.120 --> 01:08:20.040
Don’t you remember?

860
01:08:21.760 --> 01:08:23.640
I’m the psychologist at Patti’s school.

861
01:08:25.040 --> 01:08:26.120
She told me about your dreams

862
01:08:26.280 --> 01:08:28.840
and she’s very worried.

863
01:08:29.000 --> 01:08:31.640
I thought it would be
a good idea to talk...

864
01:08:40.920 --> 01:08:41.840
Forgive me.

865
01:08:45.000 --> 01:08:47.240
I’m sorry.

866
01:08:47.400 --> 01:08:50.040
I don’t know
how I could have lost my mind like that.

867
01:08:50.680 --> 01:08:52.000
Don’t worry.

868
01:08:52.160 --> 01:08:53.360
I must be a bit...

869
01:08:54.600 --> 01:08:55.840
Between sleeping badly.

870
01:08:56.480 --> 01:08:58.840
organizing Fran’s party.

871
01:08:59.000 --> 01:09:00.520
and I’m composing a song. you know.

872
01:09:00.680 --> 01:09:02.560
Heavens!
Are you going to sing?

873
01:09:03.320 --> 01:09:04.160
So it seems.

874
01:09:04.760 --> 01:09:05.480
You know.

875
01:09:05.640 --> 01:09:08.000
I have a friend who’s a big fan of yours.

876
01:09:18.560 --> 01:09:19.760
Why are you here on your own?

877
01:09:20.880 --> 01:09:22.000
Your birthday present.

878
01:09:23.000 --> 01:09:24.280
Is it a song?

879
01:09:24.440 --> 01:09:26.280
No. Me. sing?

880
01:09:29.200 --> 01:09:30.960
How long since I told you I love you?

881
01:09:33.160 --> 01:09:35.600
-Not since this morning.
-Too long.

882
01:09:37.280 --> 01:09:38.120
I love you.

883
01:09:47.120 --> 01:09:49.440
I’ll see what Marley wants.
He’s being a nuisance.

884
01:09:59.720 --> 01:10:00.720
The cake’s ready.

885
01:10:00.880 --> 01:10:01.960
Does your father know?

886
01:10:02.120 --> 01:10:05.200
-Please. we’re professionals.
-You followed my recipe?

887
01:10:05.360 --> 01:10:07.560
-Word by word.
-And it’s amazing.

888
01:10:07.720 --> 01:10:10.080
Most important.
is it very. very. well hidden?

889
01:10:10.240 --> 01:10:12.640
-In my room.
-Where no one can enter!

890
01:10:12.800 --> 01:10:15.080
OK. here’s the plan.
In the middle of the party

891
01:10:15.240 --> 01:10:16.360
I’ll sing my song.

892
01:10:16.520 --> 01:10:19.080
when I finish. you turn off the lights
and bring out the cake.

893
01:10:19.600 --> 01:10:20.400
-OK?
-Perfect.

894
01:10:20.560 --> 01:10:21.480
OK. come on.

895
01:10:22.440 --> 01:10:25.160
Thank you for being
the best stepmother in the world.

896
01:10:25.320 --> 01:10:28.920
No. it’s easy when you have
the best stepdaughters in the world.

897
01:10:32.880 --> 01:10:38.560
You don’t say anything now
and I just want to scream.

898
01:10:38.720 --> 01:10:43.400
without wanting to. I’m letting you fly.

899
01:10:46.000 --> 01:10:51.680
It’s a bit late for stirring up blood

900
01:10:51.840 --> 01:10:56.600
and I forgot how to stop
a long time ago.

901
01:10:59.240 --> 01:11:04.920
You have something within you.
I have seen it shine.

902
01:11:05.080 --> 01:11:08.080
but you run away

903
01:11:08.960 --> 01:11:11.800
and run away.

904
01:11:12.240 --> 01:11:18.040
Miss me.
don’t fail me this time.

905
01:11:18.200 --> 01:11:23.240
because I don’t know if I’ll be back.

906
01:11:25.600 --> 01:11:28.360
You have something within you.

907
01:11:28.520 --> 01:11:31.120
if you don’t stop running away

908
01:11:31.280 --> 01:11:37.040
I’m going to leave you
and I won’t come back.

909
01:11:41.040 --> 01:11:43.040
Bravo! Bravo!

910
01:11:54.440 --> 01:11:57.160
Hey. I didn’t see you!
When did you get here?

911
01:11:57.320 --> 01:11:59.880
Just in time to see you sing.
I’ll introduce you.

912
01:12:00.040 --> 01:12:02.000
-Your biggest fan.
-Thank you for inviting us.

913
01:12:02.400 --> 01:12:04.400
You were wonderful.

914
01:12:04.560 --> 01:12:06.240
Thank you for coming.

915
01:12:10.520 --> 01:12:13.600
Your face looks familiar.
Have we met?

916
01:12:14.680 --> 01:12:18.160
I was here a long time ago.
investigating a case of suicide.

917
01:12:18.320 --> 01:12:20.440
I didn’t tell you.
my friend is a policeman.

918
01:12:25.320 --> 01:12:27.840
You mean a case of suicide
in this house?

919
01:12:29.040 --> 01:12:32.160
Yes. a woman hanged herself on that tree.

920
01:12:32.600 --> 01:12:33.640
A messy love affair.

921
01:12:37.080 --> 01:12:38.160
It’s time for the cake.

922
01:12:38.960 --> 01:12:41.320
For he’s a jolly good fellow.

923
01:12:41.480 --> 01:12:43.720
for he’s a jolly good fellow.

924
01:12:43.880 --> 01:12:46.680
for he’s a jolly good fellow.

925
01:12:46.840 --> 01:12:48.880
and so say all of us!

926
01:12:49.040 --> 01:12:51.160
And so say all of us.

927
01:12:51.800 --> 01:12:52.720
Thank you!

928
01:13:04.200 --> 01:13:05.000
Hey.

929
01:13:06.280 --> 01:13:07.160
the cake is delicious.

930
01:13:07.320 --> 01:13:08.120
Thank you.

931
01:13:08.280 --> 01:13:09.920
-Did you make it?
-Of course.

932
01:13:10.880 --> 01:13:13.720
-You’re lying to us.
-Of course!

933
01:13:15.760 --> 01:13:17.840
Come on. I want to tell you something.

934
01:13:18.600 --> 01:13:19.400
Come on.

935
01:13:27.520 --> 01:13:28.280
Tell me.

936
01:13:29.560 --> 01:13:31.400
That man. the policeman.

937
01:13:32.760 --> 01:13:34.120
he asked me things about you.

938
01:13:36.000 --> 01:13:36.880
About me?

939
01:13:37.520 --> 01:13:38.320
When?

940
01:13:39.440 --> 01:13:40.520
Fifteen years ago.

941
01:13:43.080 --> 01:13:44.000
That’s impossible.

942
01:13:45.440 --> 01:13:46.880
He wanted to know if I knew you.

943
01:13:48.480 --> 01:13:50.000
and how you were getting on with Dad.

944
01:13:51.960 --> 01:13:55.640
Child. fifteen years ago
you still hadn’t been born.

945
01:13:55.800 --> 01:13:59.240
Rosa! You’re missing
the best of the party!

946
01:13:59.400 --> 01:14:00.760
We’re going to drink a toast!

947
01:14:04.600 --> 01:14:06.000
Where did you get that mask. Patti?

948
01:14:12.880 --> 01:14:13.680
Patti?

949
01:14:20.160 --> 01:14:22.480
So someone killed themself here.

950
01:14:23.120 --> 01:14:25.080
Fifteen years ago.
Don’t you remember?

951
01:14:29.440 --> 01:14:30.320
It’s true.

952
01:14:31.440 --> 01:14:32.440
I’d forgotten.

953
01:14:33.800 --> 01:14:35.280
A woman killed herself here.

954
01:14:37.400 --> 01:14:38.240
A woman?

955
01:14:40.960 --> 01:14:41.800
What woman?

956
01:14:44.200 --> 01:14:45.000
Who?

957
01:14:46.760 --> 01:14:47.560
It was you.

958
01:14:48.720 --> 01:14:50.120
You hanged yourself on the tree.

959
01:14:55.280 --> 01:14:56.520
Did you tell them my dream?

960
01:14:58.680 --> 01:14:59.920
It wasn’t a dream.

961
01:15:01.400 --> 01:15:02.360
Isn’t that right. Ana?

962
01:15:03.600 --> 01:15:05.320
For the great Rosa Martín.

963
01:15:05.960 --> 01:15:07.680
also known as "The Hanged Woman".

964
01:15:08.320 --> 01:15:10.600
who. doing honor to her stage name.

965
01:15:10.760 --> 01:15:13.400
hanged herself from that beautiful tree
fifteen years ago

966
01:15:13.560 --> 01:15:17.200
and then contrived to murder me
in the same way.

967
01:15:20.080 --> 01:15:21.360
For the Hanged Woman!

968
01:15:21.520 --> 01:15:23.080
For the Hanged Woman!

969
01:15:24.400 --> 01:15:25.800
This is a joke. isn’t it?

970
01:15:26.760 --> 01:15:28.240
What kind of fucking joke is this?

971
01:15:30.040 --> 01:15:30.840
Fran?

972
01:15:31.840 --> 01:15:33.080
I didn’t kill anybody. Fran.

973
01:15:34.840 --> 01:15:35.960
Yes. you did.

974
01:15:38.800 --> 01:15:39.840
You killed yourself.

975
01:15:41.680 --> 01:15:43.920
you killed Oscar. Marley.

976
01:15:45.600 --> 01:15:46.960
and you killed Ana too!

977
01:15:49.160 --> 01:15:50.120
But Ana is there!

978
01:15:52.040 --> 01:15:52.880
And Marley!

979
01:15:54.200 --> 01:15:55.400
Don’t you hear Marley barking?

980
01:15:55.560 --> 01:15:57.200
Marley? Marley?

981
01:16:10.720 --> 01:16:12.240
Fran. it wasn’t me.

982
01:16:12.400 --> 01:16:13.760
Fran. it wasn’t me!

983
01:16:23.760 --> 01:16:24.680
This isn’t happening.

984
01:16:25.440 --> 01:16:27.800
This isn’t happening.

985
01:16:28.560 --> 01:16:29.600
Go away!

986
01:16:39.680 --> 01:16:40.600
Don’t be scared.

987
01:16:40.760 --> 01:16:42.760
You’re dreaming. we’re both dreaming.

988
01:16:42.920 --> 01:16:43.840
Come on. run!

989
01:16:50.480 --> 01:16:52.120
-Where are we going?
-To my room.

990
01:16:52.680 --> 01:16:53.480
Run!

991
01:16:53.640 --> 01:16:55.720
-It’s time.
-It has to be now.

992
01:16:56.400 --> 01:16:57.840
It’s almost the time she died.

993
01:17:01.040 --> 01:17:01.760
Run. open the door!

994
01:17:01.920 --> 01:17:02.720
I can’t.

995
01:17:02.880 --> 01:17:04.120
You have the key in your hand.

996
01:17:09.560 --> 01:17:10.320
Patti!

997
01:17:28.520 --> 01:17:29.480
Who are you?

998
01:17:37.240 --> 01:17:38.720
You aren’t Patti’s psychologist.

999
01:17:39.520 --> 01:17:40.440
No.

1000
01:17:41.160 --> 01:17:42.160
I am Patti.

1001
01:17:46.080 --> 01:17:47.120
Patti is a child.

1002
01:17:48.640 --> 01:17:49.440
I was.

1003
01:17:50.960 --> 01:17:52.200
Fifteen years ago.

1004
01:17:53.880 --> 01:17:54.640
No.

1005
01:17:55.040 --> 01:17:56.000
Patti

1006
01:17:56.480 --> 01:17:57.640
is out there.

1007
01:17:58.320 --> 01:17:59.200
Open the door

1008
01:18:00.280 --> 01:18:01.320
and you’ll see reality.

1009
01:18:47.680 --> 01:18:48.480
Fran!

1010
01:18:50.360 --> 01:18:51.120
Fran!

1011
01:18:53.000 --> 01:18:53.840
Where’s Fran?

1012
01:19:13.000 --> 01:19:13.760
Fran!

1013
01:19:19.680 --> 01:19:20.720
What have you done to him?

1014
01:19:23.480 --> 01:19:24.800
You did it.

1015
01:19:26.480 --> 01:19:28.000
You turned him into this.

1016
01:19:29.560 --> 01:19:31.120
You’re not Patti!

1017
01:19:40.440 --> 01:19:44.680
Fifteen years ago you tricked me
into freeing you from the tree.

1018
01:19:45.800 --> 01:19:48.760
You promised you’d leave.
but instead you killed my mother.

1019
01:19:48.920 --> 01:19:49.920
No!

1020
01:19:51.600 --> 01:19:53.360
And then you possessed my father.

1021
01:19:53.520 --> 01:19:55.400
taking advantage
of his weakest moment.

1022
01:20:06.480 --> 01:20:08.840
You created a dream world in his mind

1023
01:20:09.880 --> 01:20:13.360
in which you’re happy. time doesn’t pass.
everyone adores you...

1024
01:20:14.680 --> 01:20:17.360
For fifteen years you controlled his will

1025
01:20:17.520 --> 01:20:19.640
so he didn’t want to see anyone
or leave the house.

1026
01:20:19.800 --> 01:20:20.680
He merely

1027
01:20:22.360 --> 01:20:23.200
subsists.

1028
01:20:24.360 --> 01:20:25.200
sleeps.

1029
01:20:26.400 --> 01:20:27.160
dreams

1030
01:20:27.840 --> 01:20:28.800
of your ideal world.

1031
01:20:30.840 --> 01:20:31.640
And all that.

1032
01:20:33.480 --> 01:20:34.440
all that is killing him.

1033
01:20:34.600 --> 01:20:36.960
you are killing him.

1034
01:20:38.640 --> 01:20:39.680
But you don’t realize.

1035
01:20:40.640 --> 01:20:44.080
because after all this time
you are trapped in your own fantasy.

1036
01:20:44.240 --> 01:20:46.040
in your own obsession.

1037
01:20:47.640 --> 01:20:48.640
And really.

1038
01:20:49.280 --> 01:20:53.480
you’re not married to him.
and you’re not a world famous artist.

1039
01:20:56.720 --> 01:20:58.720
You’re just a parasite.

1040
01:21:02.440 --> 01:21:05.680
Your father deserved that.
and a lot more.

1041
01:21:06.280 --> 01:21:07.280
But my mother didn’t.

1042
01:21:10.840 --> 01:21:11.840
And neither did Janis.

1043
01:21:14.200 --> 01:21:16.360
She killed herself five years ago.

1044
01:21:17.800 --> 01:21:21.280
Neither she nor he
ever got over my mother’s death.

1045
01:21:22.760 --> 01:21:23.560
You know.

1046
01:21:24.560 --> 01:21:27.200
it was hard for me to understand
what was happening inside his head.

1047
01:21:29.000 --> 01:21:33.400
And even harder to infiltrate the fantasy
in which you’d trapped him.

1048
01:21:38.400 --> 01:21:39.720
You’ve grown up a lot. Patti.

1049
01:21:43.160 --> 01:21:43.960
Congratulations.

1050
01:21:45.480 --> 01:21:47.160
you fooled me very well.

1051
01:21:48.880 --> 01:21:50.600
I had a very good teacher.

1052
01:21:51.680 --> 01:21:52.560
Thank you.

1053
01:21:53.320 --> 01:21:54.320
I don’t mean you.

1054
01:22:01.560 --> 01:22:02.440
Why are you here?

1055
01:22:03.680 --> 01:22:05.040
To help me transition?

1056
01:22:06.960 --> 01:22:08.760
We’ve thought of something better.

1057
01:22:11.840 --> 01:22:12.600
Do you like it?

1058
01:22:14.800 --> 01:22:15.760
Begoña’s idea.

1059
01:22:16.520 --> 01:22:18.400
It wasn’t easy to find this.

1060
01:22:21.120 --> 01:22:26.200
Pretty. so pretty. my beautiful Oscar.

1061
01:22:26.360 --> 01:22:31.800
Pretty. so pretty. my gentle Oscar.

1062
01:22:31.960 --> 01:22:34.440
Fly sweetly.

1063
01:22:34.600 --> 01:22:35.360
Fly blue.

1064
01:22:35.520 --> 01:22:38.000
Fran. this isn’t happening.

1065
01:22:38.160 --> 01:22:40.480
I’m your rose of sugar.

1066
01:22:40.640 --> 01:22:42.400
Fran. you’re dreaming.

1067
01:22:43.120 --> 01:22:45.360
I’m your rose of honey.

1068
01:22:45.520 --> 01:22:46.600
We’re both dreaming.

1069
01:22:46.760 --> 01:22:47.640
Look at me.

1070
01:24:22.680 --> 01:24:23.600
Dad. that’s it.

1071
01:24:25.440 --> 01:24:26.400
